Settling a thread leaves the timer where it was.
A thread alone on the processor that loses its units would run on to a tick set for it alone;
the timer is set past a tick only while no change since has brought that tick forward.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer is set past a tick an unmarked change brought forward

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -209,7 +209,6 @@ static uint8_t thread_queue(const struct thread *t, uint32_t balance)
 static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
-    core->wake_stale = true;
     account_refill(t);
     uint8_t queue = thread_queue(t, t->balance);
     if (queue != t->queue) {
